# Extensibility (L1 / L2 / L3)

## L1 — Static (boot)

- Brand values (colors, fonts, logo, SEO) live in `config/extensibility/static.config.json`, merged with server `staticConfig` from `GET /api/uiMetdata`.
- Use `useStaticConfig()` / CSS variables (`var(--brand-primary)`) — never hardcode hex in page configs.
- Gate optional features with `condition.flag` or `<FeatureGate flag="enableBlog">`.

## L2 — Dynamic (runtime)

- Navigation, action descriptors, and slots: `dynamicConfig` on the same UI metadata document, merged with bundled defaults.
- Use `useNavigation(zone)` for chrome nav; do not hardcode nav arrays.
- UI actions must reference bundled `ServiceRegistry` handlers (`package::serviceId`) or built-in navigate/popup — no arbitrary JS from server.
- Add `<ExtensionSlotHost slot-id="..." />` at extension points.

## L1/L2 persistence (Supabase / PostgreSQL)

- Page patches, `staticConfig`, and `dynamicConfig` are stored together in `ui_metadata.body_json`.
- Requires `APP_PERSISTENCE_PROVIDER=postgres` and `SPRING_DATASOURCE_*` (Supabase).
- **Write (only):** `POST /api/uiMetdata/save` — include any of `packages`, `staticConfig`, `dynamicConfig`, `i18nBundles`; omitted/empty sections are merged with the stored document (partial saves supported).
- **`i18nBundles`:** per-locale strings merged into vue-i18n. Use **nested** keys (preferred) `{ "hospital": { "brandTitle": "..." } }` or flat `hospital.brandTitle` (expanded on the client). Components need `i18nKey: "hospital.brandTitle"`, not hardcoded `text`.
- **Delete:** `DELETE /api/uiMetdata` or `DELETE /api/uiMetdata/default` (soft-delete singleton row).
- **Read:** `GET /api/uiMetdata` (permitAll). No server restart; hard-refresh the browser after save.
- Merge matches components by **`id`** — ids must be unique per config file (`ui-component-ids.mdc`, `npm run check:ui-ids`).

## L3 — Server

- All writes that support hooks call `ExtensionHookInvoker.runBefore` / `runAfter` with key `METHOD /api/path`.
- Register hooks in `HospitalExtensionHooks`; list routes in `extension/endpoint_map.json`.
- Admin ops: `POST /api/v1/admin/extensions/reload`, `GET .../map`, `GET .../hooks` (not for L1/L2 JSON).
- Reroute only to allowlisted URLs; no PHI in hook logs.

## HTTP

- Browser → Spring only via `URLRegistry` / `apiClient` (no raw `fetch` to API except extensibility loaders).

## Packages

- Types/schemas: `@saas-builder/extensibility-contract`
- Vue integration: `@saas-builder/extensibility-vue`
